args.summary:
Fixed the stale SigV4 headers issue (CVE-2026-86409) by adding an `else` clause to clear the `CURLAUTH_AWS_SIGV4` bit from `data->set.httpauth` when `CURLOPT_AWS_SIGV4` is set to NULL.

**Root cause:** In `lib/setopt.c`, the `CURLOPT_AWS_SIGV4` case (lines 2060-2072) only set the auth bit when a non-NULL string was provided, but never cleared it when the option was set to NULL. This caused a subsequent transfer on the same handle to still send an `Authorization: AWS4-HMAC-SHA256` header.

**Fix:** Added an `else` branch that clears the auth bit using the same pattern as `CURLOPT_HTTPSIG_ALGORITHM` (lines 1069-1072):
```c
if(CURL_EASY_STR(data, STRING_AWS_SIGV4))
  s->httpauth = CURLAUTH_AWS_SIGV4;
else
  s->httpauth &= ~(uint32_t)CURLAUTH_AWS_SIGV4;
```

All 25 nearby AWS_SIGV4 tests now pass, including the regression test1978.

