rows.summary_agent:
Fixed CVE-2026-8924 by stripping trailing dots from the cookie domain before the Public Suffix List (PSL) check in `lib/cookie.c`.

**Root cause:** The `is_public_suffix()` function was checking the cookie domain against the PSL without first normalizing it by removing trailing dots. A malicious server could set a cookie with `Domain=co.uk.` (note the trailing dot), which would bypass the PSL check because "co.uk." doesn't match the public suffix "co.uk" in the list. This allowed "super cookies" to be scoped to unrelated third-party domains.

**Fix:** Added a loop in `is_public_suffix()` (lines 783-785) that strips trailing dots from `co->domain` before the PSL comparison:
```c
/* Strip trailing dots from cookie domain for PSL check */
while(clen && co->domain[clen - 1] == '.')
  clen--;
```

The fix is minimal, follows curl's C89 style (2-space indent, existing helpers), and passes all 30 regression tests including test1629.

