steps.thought:
Let me look at the test failure more carefully. The test shows that when using a .netrc file with a proxy and following redirects, the credentials from the first host (site.example) are being sent to the second host (numbertwo.example). 

Looking at the code in http.c around line 842-847:
```c
if(Curl_auth_allowed_to_host(data)
#ifndef CURL_DISABLE_NETRC
   || conn->bits.netrc
#endif
)
  result = output_auth_headers(data, conn, authhost, request, path, FALSE);
else
  authhost->done = TRUE;
```

The issue is that when `conn->bits.netrc` is set, it bypasses the `Curl_auth_allowed_to_host` check and sends credentials to any host. But the netrc credentials should only be sent to the specific hos

